Schema migrations.

The database URL comes from DATABASE_URL in backend/.env, via
alembic/env.py — never from alembic.ini, which has no URL in it. Switching
between the local Postgres and Neon is that one variable, the same one the
application reads.

Run from backend/ with PYTHONPATH=. so `app` is importable.

  Set up a database that has never been migrated
      alembic upgrade head

  After changing a model
      alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"
      # read the generated file before applying it — autogenerate is good at
      # added and dropped columns, and poor at renames, which it will
      # cheerfully emit as a drop plus an add, losing the data in between
      alembic upgrade head

  Check whether the models and the database have drifted apart
      alembic check

  Undo the last migration
      alembic downgrade -1

The app no longer creates tables at startup. create_all only ever created
MISSING TABLES — it silently ignored new columns on tables that already
existed, which is how five columns came to be added by hand in psql with no
record of it anywhere. A database that has not been migrated will now fail
loudly on a missing table instead of quietly on a missing column.

The baseline revision was generated against an empty scratch database so it
contains the full CREATE, then both existing databases were stamped with it,
since their schemas already matched. Nothing was recreated and no data moved.
